00:09:47.600 --> 00:09:51.360
perfect product. Aim for something

00:09:48.880 --> 00:09:53.519
useful. Either a tiny tool or an app or

00:09:51.360 --> 00:09:56.000
a guide. Something that solves a real

00:09:53.519 --> 00:09:57.519
problem. I personally found it best if I

00:09:56.000 --> 00:09:59.920
focused on building something for

00:09:57.519 --> 00:10:01.920
myself. Step two would be to ship it

00:09:59.920 --> 00:10:03.600
publicly. Shipping is non-negotiable.

00:10:01.920 --> 00:10:05.760
Post it on Twitter, on YouTube, on

00:10:03.600 --> 00:10:07.839
Reddit, on Tik Tok, wherever you think

00:10:05.760 --> 00:10:09.920
your potential clients hang out. Most

00:10:07.839 --> 00:10:11.440
projects don't fail because they're bad.

00:10:09.920 --> 00:10:13.600
They fail because nobody ever heard of

00:10:11.440 --> 00:10:14.959
them. Step three is to get feedback. Do

00:10:13.600 --> 00:10:16.720
people use your tool? Do they ask

00:10:14.959 --> 00:10:18.079
questions? Do they come back? Do they

00:10:16.720 --> 00:10:20.000
complain? [music] Gather all the

00:10:18.079 --> 00:10:22.240
feedback and use it to improve the

00:10:20.000 --> 00:10:24.480
product. Step four would be to add

00:10:22.240 --> 00:10:26.240
monetization early. Add a pay tier. This

00:10:24.480 --> 00:10:28.399
is the real validation strategy. Do

00:10:26.240 --> 00:10:30.160
people pay for a product? If they do,

00:10:28.399 --> 00:10:31.519
then you have something valuable. The

00:10:30.160 --> 00:10:33.440
goal isn't to get rich at this [music]

00:10:31.519 --> 00:10:35.760
point. The goal is to validate that the

00:10:33.440 --> 00:10:38.240
problem you are trying to solve is worth

00:10:35.760 --> 00:10:40.079
paying for. Step five is to decide if

00:10:38.240 --> 00:10:42.240
you want to double down or move on.

00:10:40.079 --> 00:10:44.000
After a few weeks or months, make a

00:10:42.240 --> 00:10:45.839
clear decision. If the product shows

00:10:44.000 --> 00:10:47.920
traction, then double down. If it's

00:10:45.839 --> 00:10:49.600
flat, move on to the next idea without

00:10:47.920 --> 00:10:51.360
feeling any [music] guilt. Every project

00:10:49.600 --> 00:10:53.519
teaches you something, even the ones

00:10:51.360 --> 00:10:55.920
that fail. So we can summarize the loop

00:10:53.519 --> 00:10:58.160
as building, shipping, get feedback,

00:10:55.920 --> 00:10:59.920
monetize, decide, [music] and repeat

00:10:58.160 --> 00:11:01.600
until something works. Once you find

00:10:59.920 --> 00:11:03.760
something that's working, the next step

00:11:01.600 --> 00:11:05.680
is to reduce how much it depends on you.

00:11:03.760 --> 00:11:07.680
Automate what you can, simplify the

00:11:05.680 --> 00:11:09.360
product, and remove yourself from the

00:11:07.680 --> 00:11:11.839
day-to-day operations as much as

00:11:09.360 --> 00:11:13.760
possible. That does two things. One, it

00:11:11.839 --> 00:11:15.440
frees up your time to work on the next

00:11:13.760 --> 00:11:17.600
idea. [music] And two, it makes the

00:11:15.440 --> 00:11:19.440
project easier to sell later because it

00:11:17.600 --> 00:11:21.519
can run on its own. For example, I have

00:11:19.440 --> 00:11:23.920
my coding course. I worked on it years

00:11:21.519 --> 00:11:25.360
ago, built it, launched it, and now it

00:11:23.920 --> 00:11:27.600
brings in passive revenue even [music]

00:11:25.360 --> 00:11:29.839
if I'm not spending time on it and I can

00:11:27.600 --> 00:11:31.440
focus on building the next product.

